{
  "name": "sugar_mill_ruin",
  "version": 2,
  "introduced_by": "lowmouth",
  "notes": "The old sugar house, drawn as a roofless ruin: brick walls 5.5 m high on a 14 x 24 m footprint with stepped gable ends 9 m high, an arched cart door on local -Z and a square brick chimney 17.5 m tall behind the back wall (+Z). Inside are the kettle battery with five rusted kettles, the cane mill and its flywheel and a boiler; give it an age.",
